            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0662" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.75 National Telephone Company/71:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain (Laughlin) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-03T16:00:00+00:00">December 3, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 3—1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. Rock is informed by a source close
                    to Government that if the American press were immediately to launch a rumor that
                    I be at once withdrawn thus provoking a state of “semi-diplomatic rupture” in
                    the event that Spain maintained an <hi rendition="#italic">intransigeant</hi>
                    attitude the peseta might react to such a statement thereby exercising an
                    important and essential influence on the Spanish position.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Laughlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
